From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 12:05:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: turing-rk1: enable the util command set

The util image is the RK1's recovery and bring-up tool: a u-boot flashed
to eMMC and driven at the prompt over the module's UART, for a board
whose OS will not boot or whose disks need work before one exists. Add
the commands that job needs beyond a booting image.

  * bootmenu  -- pick a boot target interactively instead of typing a
    bootcmd, which is what an operator on a serial line actually wants.
  * memtest   -- a DRAM walk before trusting a module.
  * md5sum,
    sha1sum   -- hash an image in RAM before it is written to a disk,
    and hash it back off the disk afterwards. Writing several GiB to an
    NVMe over a link that has no integrity check of its own is exactly
    where a silent corruption goes unnoticed.
  * wget      -- pull that image from an HTTP server. tftp is already
    here, but a plain web server is one less daemon to stand up on the
    host driving the recovery.
  * read,
    write     -- raw block access to a partition, for dumping a header
    or restoring one without a filesystem in the way.

The image-writing path itself needs nothing new: gzwrite comes with
CONFIG_CMD_UNZIP, which CONFIG_CMD_BOOTI already selects on arm64, so
`gzwrite nvme 0 ${loadaddr} ${filesize}` decompresses and writes a
gzipped image to the disk in one step.

Autoboot is left alone. Unlike a tool streamed into RAM over maskrom,
this one is flashed, so it has to stay able to boot the module normally
between recovery sessions; the interruptible delay is what makes it safe
to leave installed.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 configs/turing-rk1-rk3588_defconfig | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/configs/turing-rk1-rk3588_defconfig b/configs/turing-rk1-rk3588_defconfig
index 347a36a2..0e556463 100644
--- a/configs/turing-rk1-rk3588_defconfig
+++ b/configs/turing-rk1-rk3588_defconfig
@@ -23,17 +23,24 @@ CONFIG_DISPLAY_BOARDINFO_LATE=y
 CONFIG_SPL_MAX_SIZE=0x40000
 # CONFIG_SPL_RAW_IMAGE_SUPPORT is not set
 CONFIG_SPL_ATF=y
+CONFIG_CMD_BOOTMENU=y
+CONFIG_CMD_MD5SUM=y
+CONFIG_CMD_MEMTEST=y
+CONFIG_CMD_SHA1SUM=y
 CONFIG_CMD_GPIO=y
 CONFIG_CMD_GPT=y
 CONFIG_CMD_I2C=y
 CONFIG_CMD_MMC=y
 CONFIG_CMD_PCI=y
+CONFIG_CMD_READ=y
 # CONFIG_CMD_SATA is not set
 CONFIG_CMD_USB=y
 CONFIG_CMD_ROCKUSB=y
 CONFIG_CMD_USB_MASS_STORAGE=y
+CONFIG_CMD_WRITE=y
 CONFIG_CMD_TFTPPUT=y
 CONFIG_CMD_TFTPSRV=y
+CONFIG_CMD_WGET=y
 CONFIG_CMD_REGULATOR=y
 # CONFIG_SPL_DOS_PARTITION is not set
 CONFIG_SPL_OF_CONTROL=y
